WEBVTT

00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:15.477
It's satisfying to know
all our food has been
dumped down a hole.

00:00:15.651 --> 00:00:18.654
- [dragon shrieks]
- They're not eating
any of it.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.617
[shudders]

00:00:28.011 --> 00:00:30.144
[growling]

00:00:33.103 --> 00:00:35.758
- [gasps]
- What is that?

00:00:41.198 --> 00:00:42.808
[roars]

00:00:42.982 --> 00:00:45.855
All right, bud, we got
to get out of here... now!

00:00:54.907 --> 00:00:59.085
[Astrid] No, it totally
makes sense. It's like
a giant beehive.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:00.957
They're the workers
and that's their queen.

00:01:01.131 --> 00:01:03.525
It controls them.
Let's find your dad.

00:01:03.699 --> 00:01:05.004
No! No.

00:01:05.179 --> 00:01:09.052
No, not yet.
They'll kill Toothless.

00:01:09.226 --> 00:01:12.447
We have to think this
through carefully.

00:01:12.621 --> 00:01:15.624
Hiccup, we just discovered
the dragons' nest,

00:01:15.798 --> 00:01:18.714
the thing we've been after
since Vikings
first sailed here,

00:01:18.888 --> 00:01:20.846
and you want
to keep it a secret?

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.110
To protect your pet dragon?
Are you serious?

00:01:26.156 --> 00:01:27.201
Yes.

00:01:34.904 --> 00:01:37.602
OK. Then what do we do?

00:01:37.776 --> 00:01:41.084
Just give me until tomorrow.
I'll figure something out.

00:01:41.954 --> 00:01:43.042
OK.

00:01:44.696 --> 00:01:45.871
That's for kidnapping me.

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:49.135
[growls]

00:01:53.096 --> 00:01:55.620
That's
for everything else.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.152
What are you looking at?

00:02:07.719 --> 00:02:11.897
[crowd] Hiccup! Hiccup!
Hiccup! Hiccup!

00:02:14.291 --> 00:02:18.077
Well, I can show my face
in public again! [laughs]

00:02:19.905 --> 00:02:23.126
If someone had told me
that in a few short weeks

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.563
Hiccup would go
from, well,

00:02:25.737 --> 00:02:28.044
being, uh, Hiccup

00:02:28.218 --> 00:02:31.090
to placing first
in dragon training,

00:02:31.265 --> 00:02:35.312
I'd have tied him to a mast
and shipped him off
for fear he'd gone mad!

00:02:35.486 --> 00:02:39.534
- [cheering]
- And you know it! [laughs]

00:02:39.708 --> 00:02:44.756
But here we are.
And no one is more surprised

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.803
or more proud than I am.

00:02:47.977 --> 00:02:51.981
Today, my boy
becomes a Viking.

00:02:52.155 --> 00:02:54.940
- Today,
he becomes one of us!
- [crowd cheers]

00:02:59.118 --> 00:03:00.990
Be careful
with that dragon.

00:03:01.164 --> 00:03:02.992
It's not the dragon
I'm worried about.

00:03:03.166 --> 00:03:04.472
[Astrid] What are you
going to do?

00:03:04.646 --> 00:03:07.126
Put an end to this.
I have to try.

00:03:08.389 --> 00:03:11.566
Astrid,
if something goes wrong,

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:14.177
just make sure they don't
find Toothless.

00:03:14.351 --> 00:03:18.137
I will. Just promise me
it won't go wrong.

00:03:18.312 --> 00:03:22.316
It's time, Hiccup.
Knock 'em dead.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:25.188
[crowd chanting, applause]

00:03:28.844 --> 00:03:30.236
Yeah! Show 'em how it's done.

00:03:31.281 --> 00:03:33.892
Hiccup! Hiccup!
Hiccup! Hiccup!

00:03:45.426 --> 00:03:47.384
Hmm, I'd have gone
for the hammer.

00:03:49.778 --> 00:03:51.345
[deep breath, exhales]

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:52.781
I'm ready.

00:03:58.177 --> 00:04:00.310
- [shrieking]
- [crowd gasps]

00:04:09.754 --> 00:04:11.321
[growling]

00:04:17.066 --> 00:04:19.938
[man] Go on, Hiccup.
Give it to him!

00:04:23.899 --> 00:04:25.248
What is he doing?

00:04:25.422 --> 00:04:27.032
[murmuring]

00:04:28.294 --> 00:04:31.080
Hey, it's OK. It's OK.

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:40.132
I'm not one of them.

00:04:44.354 --> 00:04:46.008
- [gasps]
- What's he thinking?

00:04:46.182 --> 00:04:48.140
- Stop the fight.
- [Hiccup] No!

00:04:48.314 --> 00:04:50.969
I need you all
to see this.

00:04:52.362 --> 00:04:54.146
They're not
what we think they are.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.366
We don't have to kill them.

00:04:57.976 --> 00:05:00.326
I said, stop the fight!

00:05:02.154 --> 00:05:03.417
- [crowd gasps]
- Aaah!

00:05:07.943 --> 00:05:08.770
Out of my way!

00:05:08.944 --> 00:05:10.424
Hiccup!

00:05:12.904 --> 00:05:15.254
[growling]

00:05:19.955 --> 00:05:21.260
Aaah!

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.402
Hiccup!

00:05:35.449 --> 00:05:36.275
[growls]

00:05:38.843 --> 00:05:40.279
This way!

00:05:47.112 --> 00:05:48.853
- [snarling]
- [Toothless divebombs]

00:05:49.027 --> 00:05:51.029
[shrieks]

00:05:53.945 --> 00:05:56.426
[clamoring]

00:06:00.561 --> 00:06:02.127
Night Fury!

00:06:09.308 --> 00:06:10.875
[roars]

00:06:20.406 --> 00:06:22.321
All right, Toothless, go.
Get out of here.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.456
- Go, go!
- [Astrid] Stoick, no!

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:29.459
- Dad, he won't hurt you!
- [growls]

00:06:29.633 --> 00:06:32.375
No, don't!
You're only making it worse!

00:06:33.202 --> 00:06:34.464
Toothless, stop!

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:37.989
No! No!

00:06:39.643 --> 00:06:41.863
- [moans]
- [panting]

00:06:42.037 --> 00:06:43.081
[man] Get him!

00:06:46.302 --> 00:06:48.913
No, no! Please don't hurt him!

00:06:49.087 --> 00:06:50.436
Please don't hurt him.

00:06:55.093 --> 00:06:57.052
[grunting]

00:06:57.226 --> 00:06:59.228
Put it with the others.

00:07:02.013 --> 00:07:04.276
I should have known.
I should have seen the signs.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.540
- Dad?
- We had a deal!

00:07:06.714 --> 00:07:10.544
I know we did.
That was before...
Aw, it's all so messed up.

00:07:10.718 --> 00:07:14.156
So everything in the ring,
a trick? A lie?

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:18.421
I screwed up.
I should have told you
before now. I just...

00:07:18.595 --> 00:07:20.379
Take this out on me,
be mad at me,

00:07:20.554 --> 00:07:22.468
but please, just
don't hurt Toothless.

00:07:22.643 --> 00:07:25.471
The dragon? That's what
you're worried about?

00:07:25.646 --> 00:07:27.604
Not the people
you almost killed?

00:07:27.778 --> 00:07:30.041
He was protecting me!
He's not dangerous.

00:07:30.215 --> 00:07:32.130
They've killed
hundreds of us!

00:07:32.304 --> 00:07:34.263
And we've killed
thousands of them!

00:07:34.437 --> 00:07:37.266
They defend themselves,
that's all!

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.921
They raid us
because they have to.

00:07:40.095 --> 00:07:43.402
If they don't bring
enough food back,
they're eaten themselves.

00:07:43.577 --> 00:07:48.320
There's something else
on their island.
It's a dragon like...

00:07:48.494 --> 00:07:50.801
Their island? So
you've been to the nest?

00:07:50.975 --> 00:07:52.629
- Did I say nest?
- How did you find it?

00:07:52.803 --> 00:07:55.458
What? No, I didn't.
Toothless did.

00:07:55.632 --> 00:07:59.505
Only a dragon
can find the island.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.900
No, no, no. No, Dad.
No, please,
it's not what you think.

00:08:03.074 --> 00:08:05.990
You don't know what you're up
against. It's like nothing
you've ever seen.

00:08:06.164 --> 00:08:09.951
Dad, please. I promise you,
you can't win this one!

00:08:10.125 --> 00:08:11.996
No, Dad. No.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.434
For once in your life,
would you please
just listen to me?!

00:08:19.482 --> 00:08:23.268
You've thrown your lot in
with them.
You're not a Viking.

00:08:25.183 --> 00:08:27.403
You're not my son.

00:08:30.362 --> 00:08:31.581
Ready the ships!

